[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: ARCHITECTURE
class: custom
version: 1.0.0

[ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW]
pyramid:
  Layer 1: editor (executable)
            └── engine (static lib)
                  └── core (static lib)
                        └── common (INTERFACE)
                              └── third-party

[LAYER_HIERARCHY]
description: Dependency order (lower depends on higher)

[LAYER_COMMON]
role: Interfaces and third-party headers
provides:
  - GLM math library
  - Boost headers (json, hana, program_options, asio, test)
  - Custom data structures (fixed_vector, smart pointers)
  - Engine-wide macros and assertions
scope: Editor + Engine + Core

[LAYER_CORE]
role: Engine foundation and services
modules:
  - ecs: EnTT-based ECS with multi-world support (auto-dispatch world IDs 0-4, max 5)
  - window: Platform window management
  - resource: VFS resolver, Adapter pipeline (Assimp/stb/text), cache
  - desc: JSON descriptor system with inheritance (level→world→prefab)
  - config: Macro-based config system (CFG_VAR_DEF_*)
  - app: Application lifecycle and module system
  - video: Window abstraction layer
key_patterns:
  - Service Locator: ds::app_data_storage (type-safe DI)
  - Module System: lifecycle ordered by topological sort over module_interface::depends_on() (priority = tiebreaker only; core/core/application/include/snk/application/app_module_loader.hpp)
  - Resource System: res::tag identification, VFS protocols (res://,memory://)
  - Descriptor System: Inheritance chain, JSON serialization

[LAYER_ENGINE]
role: Gameplay and rendering systems
modules:
  - scene: Entity/prefab management, hierarchy, object transforms
  - render: Data-driven pipeline (extractors→passes), material system
  - gui: ImGui integration, editor panels
  - input: Keyboard/mouse/gamepad handling
  - game: Game-specific systems and logic hooks
render_pipeline:
  1. Extractors: Camera→render_packet (geometry, instances, lights);
     extractors live in core/engine/scene/level/ (scn_render_data_extractor.cpp
     extracts geometry and lights), NOT in a render/extractors/ dir
  2. Passes (render_pass_interface): z_prepass, opaque, skybox, transparent (OIT),
     composition, debug
  3. Output: ImGui overlay, per-camera render targets

[LAYER_EDITOR]
role: Real-time scene editing
modules:
  - editor: Main editor application
  - panels: Inspector, hierarchy, asset browser, prefab editor
  - gizmo: Transform, rotate, scale handles in viewport
  - viewport: Scene preview, camera controls
key_features:
  - Async operations (loading, cooking resources)
  - Per-camera render targets (__editor_depth_rt, etc.)
  - Live prefab preview in separate world
  - Descriptor hot-reload and validation

[MEMORY_SYSTEM]
allocators:
  - frame_allocator: Per-frame bump (resets every frame start)
  - linear_resource: Custom-scoped bump allocator
  - pool_resource: Fixed-size O(1) alloc/free
  - stack_resource: LIFO with markers
  - debug_resource: Guard bytes, leak tracking (Debug only)
hot_path_pattern:
  std::pmr::vector<T> vec(ds::frame_allocator());
  vec.reserve(estimated_size); // avoid grow-copy
  // use vec during frame
  // automatically freed at frame reset

[ECS_SYSTEM]
worlds: Independent worlds keyed by name; automatic system dispatch supports
        world IDs 0-4 (max 5, hard-coded switch in registration_dispatcher).
        Per-world component access via world_salt + bind_res<WorldID,T>.
world_order: scn::level stores worlds in std::unordered_map (HASH order).
        for_each_world does NOT preserve desc order — see CONSTRAINTS [13C].
        Editor derives parallel world arrays from the ordered world_descs vector
        (edt::derive_world_arrays), making desc order the single source of truth.
systems: All inherit ecs::system_interface (empty base), registered via
        ecs::system_factory::register_system<&fn>(name, {phase, after, before, run_in_edit}).
        The interface has no update() — per-frame logic is the registered fn; order = phase,
        then after/before, ties by the world desc system list (no type-inferred ordering).
components: POD structs, optional _component suffix
dependency_resolution: Auto via invoker<Candidate>; system fn arg types
        (entt::view, ecs::bind_res) resolved through the registry context
boot_sequence:
  module_loader.add_module(core, engine, editor)
  → register_all_services()
  → initialize_all_services() // topo-sorted by depends_on(), priority breaks ties
  → app.run() // loop.init → loop.on_step … → loop.term (term also when a step throws)
  → shutdown_all_services() // reverse order

[FRAME_LOOP]
design: docs/roadmap/design/FRAME_LOOP.md
loop: one app::loop_service (core/core/application) for every host; core_module registers it with app::frame_stage_registry
stages: begin, input, update, post_update, extract, render, ui, present (fixed, ordered; mirror of ECS phases)
  - begin: frame allocator reset (core). Nothing may run before it.
  - bodies: engine sets update/post_update (scene, input deltas) and input/extract/render/present (window, renderer) in gs_engine_frame_stages; editor sets ui (ImGui)
  - a module adds its own named stage with registry.add_stage(name, anchor, before|after, fn); same anchor = registration order; duplicate names rejected; remove_stage/clear_body on module shutdown
  - stage context: {storage, dt}; the render frame_context is a service in the storage, reset after present
camera_target: camera color_targets empty = backbuffer (draws into the default framebuffer, no present pass); a tag = texture. rnd::select_camera_target. The editor redirects backbuffer cameras to textures (edt::redirect_backbuffer_cameras)
without_editor: engine runs without editor_module; editor-only behaviour exists only as editor stages

[RESOURCE_SYSTEM]
identification: res::tag (unique resource identifier)
protocols:
  - res:// filesystem (VFS resolver)
  - memory:// runtime data
pipeline:
  VFS Resolver → Adapter (Assimp/stb/text) → Cache (weak/pinned)
async_loading: res_handle<T> with .then() callbacks
caching: Weak refs (auto-unload), pinned (persistent)

[DESCRIPTOR_SYSTEM]
format: JSON files (.desc extension)
inheritance_chain:
  level_desc
    └── world_desc (entities, systems config)
          └── prefab_desc (reusable template)
                └── prefab_node (hierarchy)
                      └── prefab_comp_node (component data)
hot_reload: Editors change descs → scene updates via binding
validation: Type checking, circular dep detection

[RENDER_PIPELINE_DETAIL]
per_camera:
  - color_targets: fixed_vector<4> MRT support
  - depth_target, tp_accum_target, tp_reveal_target
  - RT tags resolve from camera packet, fallback to legacy static tags

passes: (core/engine/render/render_system/passes/, all : render_pass_interface)
  - z_prepass: depth pre-pass
  - opaque_pass: opaque geometry
  - skybox_pass: skybox
  - transparent_pass: OIT (Order-Independent Transparency)
  - composition_pass: combine targets into final image
  - debug_pass: debug draw overlay
  ImGui editor UI is drawn by the gui system, not a render pass here.

[MODULE_LIFECYCLE]
Each module implements app::modules::module_interface:

1. register_services(): Add types to app_data_storage
   - Constructor injection, no dependencies yet

2. initialize_services(): Resolve from storage, setup
   - Topo-sorted by depends_on() (priority only breaks ties)
   - Dependencies already registered

3. shutdown_services(): Cleanup in reverse order
   - Guaranteed to run even on error

[NAMING_PATTERNS]
namespaces: 2-4 letter abbrev (ds, ecs, scn, gui, rnd, res, inp, edt, gs, cfg, wnd)
files: prefix_name.hpp/.cpp (scn_level.cpp, res_system.h)
components: _component suffix if name not self-descriptive
systems: Inherit system_interface (files like scn_level.cpp / edt_scene_editor.cpp)
variables: snake_case always; private members m_ prefix
macros: UPPER_CASE
